uestion/id #uuid "895764df-0dac-5f6c-8455-f03cf4d8e10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316635" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-4(x-5)(x-(-2))(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2) & =-4(x-5)({x}^{2}+4x+4) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+4x-5{x}^{2}-20x-20) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316635/field-1" "q-316635/field-2" "q-316635/field-3" "q-316635/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316725"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065074/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
